{"id": "qwen3-0.6b__SOLVE__prm_73f279c308", "result": "$513^2 - 487^2$\n\nWe can use the difference of squares formula: $a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)$.\n\nLet:\n- $a = 513$\n- $b = 487$\n\nThen:\n$$\n513^2 - 487^2 = (513 - 487)(513 + 487)\n$$\n\n$$\n513 - 487 = 26\n$$\n$$\n513 + 487 = 1000\n$$\n\n$$\n513^2 - 487^2 = 26 \\times 1000 = 26000\n$$\n\nAnswer: <final answer> 26000", "rc": 0, "secs": 10.08, "model": "Qwen3-0.6B-Q4_K_M.gguf", "sha256": "ac2d97712095a558e31573f62f466a3f9d93990898b0ec79d7c974c1780d524a", "finish": "stop", "seed": 0, "tokens": {"completion_tokens": 188, "prompt_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 276, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 28}}}